  "worked_solution": "Let's call $P(x)$ the polynomial shown in the diagram.\n\nThe end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is even,\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative, and\n\n- the $y$-intercept is $3,$ which means that $P(0)=3.$\n\nTherefore, of the given options, the only one that satisfies all three criteria is $y=-2{x}^{6}-{x}^{5}-2{x}^{3}-x+3.$",
